# vibe-printer.env.tmpl — rendered to /opt/vibe/env/vibe-printer.env by
# lib/enable-app.sh.
#
# Vibe Print is the suite's LAN print gateway: a caller POSTs a payload
# and a printer id, and the gateway renders and routes the job to a
# thermal, label, or office printer. Every setting it reads is prefixed
# VIBE_PRINT_ (pydantic-settings env_prefix), and it ignores every other
# variable in the environment — which is why loading shared.env and
# appliance.env alongside this file is harmless.
#
# It shares NOTHING with the rest of the stack: its own SQLite under
# /data, no Postgres role, no Redis index. See apps/vibe-printer.yml.

# --- The one credential ----------------------------------------------
# A single shared bearer secret gates the admin UI and every /v1 call.
# There is no user model behind it and no per-person login; the service
# refuses to boot if it is empty. Generated once on first enable and
# preserved across re-renders.
#
# Rotating it is a deliberate act with a blast radius, not maintenance:
# every calling system and every signed-in admin is cut off at the same
# instant. To rotate, edit the value here, then:
#     sudo docker restart vibe-printer
# and re-paste the new secret into every caller. It is also printed in
# /opt/vibe/CREDENTIALS.txt and on the console's First-login card.
VIBE_PRINT_SECRET=@VIBE_PRINT_SECRET@

# --- Storage ---------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite database, uploaded assets, backup snapshots — the entire state
# of this app. Bind-mounted from /opt/vibe/data/apps/vibe-printer/data.
VIBE_PRINT_DATA_DIR=/data

# --- Real-IP resolution ----------------------------------------------
# Which peers' forwarded-for headers are believed. On this appliance the
# only things in front of the app are the shared Caddy and the emergency
# HAProxy, both on the Docker bridge network — so loopback plus the
# RFC1918 range Docker allocates from is exactly the trust that is
# warranted. Widening it lets a caller forge the IP that the rate
# limiter and the audit log both key off.
VIBE_PRINT_TRUSTED_PROXIES=["127.0.0.1","172.16.0.0/12"]

# --- Appliance-owned ingress (do NOT start the in-app tunnel) --------
# The image bundles cloudflared and the admin UI has a Remote Access tab
# that can start a Cloudflare Tunnel as a managed child process. Do not
# use it here. The appliance's shared Caddy and its own Cloudflare
# Tunnel own public ingress; a second tunnel publishes this gateway on a
# hostname the appliance does not know about, cannot re-render, and
# cannot tear down when you leave domain mode. There is no upstream env
# var to hide that tab — this note is the control.
#
# The appliance reaches this app at:
#   domain mode          https://print.<your-domain>/  (redirects to /admin/)
#   LAN / Tailscale      http://<server-ip>:5194/      (redirects to /admin/)
#   other Vibe apps      http://vibe-printer:8080/v1   on vibe_net
#
# The bare root serves nothing — the SPA is mounted at /admin and the
# API at /v1 — so the appliance emits a 308 from / to /admin/ on both
# public surfaces (manifest routing.root_redirect).

# --- Operator-set via Settings (manifest ui blocks) ------------------
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT from this template, so an edit made on the admin
# Settings page survives the next enable — anything this file names is
# rewritten from the template on every render, while anything it does
# not name is carried forward by the merge step:
#
#   VIBE_PRINT_STORE_PAYLOADS         keep rendered payloads after print
#   VIBE_PRINT_JOB_RETENTION_DAYS     completed-job retention
#   VIBE_PRINT_AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS   audit-log retention
#   VIBE_PRINT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE  per-caller request ceiling
#   VIBE_PRINT_TIMEZONE               inherited from appliance.env's TZ
#
# NOTE the one place the appliance default differs from upstream's:
# VIBE_PRINT_STORE_PAYLOADS ships OFF here (upstream defaults it on).
# Print payloads on this appliance are receipts and client documents, so
# the default keeps only a content hash once a job has printed. Turn it
# on from Settings when you need to inspect or reprint a specific job.
#
# --- Other knobs, copy-paste only ------------------------------------
# Not surfaced in Settings; add below and `sudo docker restart
# vibe-printer`. They are preserved across re-renders because this
# template does not name them:
#
#   VIBE_PRINT_WEBHOOK_URL / VIBE_PRINT_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#       signed POST on a dead/uncertain job or an offline printer.
#   VIBE_PRINT_ENCRYPT_AT_REST / VIBE_PRINT_DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY
#       SQLCipher at rest. amd64 only — the driver has no arm64 wheel,
#       and the app degrades to unencrypted rather than refusing to
#       start, so verify it actually took effect before relying on it.
#   VIBE_PRINT_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN / VIBE_PRINT_ACCESS_AUD
#       enforce a Cloudflare Access JWT on admin routes. Only meaningful
#       if you have put Access in front of the appliance's tunnel.
